    "tessercheck_runs_count": 2,
    "final_message": "`scripts/verify story-drafting` passes every step, including both acceptance tests against the host on :9360, and there is no GAP. The work is committed as ab6664c on the current branch. Only four files changed, all of them mine.\n\n**Domain** (`<repo>/story-drafting/drafting/domain/jtbd.py`):\n- `Text` now rejects empty or whitespace-only text, so every story's given, when and then must have content.\n- I added two value objects. `StoryText` holds given, when and then, built from a `StoryTextSpec`. `StoryTexts` is built from the `RecordStoriesSpec` and turns each story text into a story in state drafted.\n- `record_stories` answers `ALREADY_RECORDED` if the job to be done already has stories and `NONE_GIVEN` if no story texts were given. Otherwise it keeps them as drafted stories and answers `RECORDED`.\n- `status` follows the rule in the language: no stories is `drafting_stories`, any drafted story is `awaiting_story_acceptance`, and otherwise it is `stories_decided`.\n- 18 tests in `test_jtbd.py` cover the three statuses, the three outcomes, rejection of empty text, and the construction round-trip.\n\n**Drafter** (`<repo>/story-drafting/drafting/adapters/gateways/template_story_drafter.py`): it returns one story text built from the job to be done:\n- given: \"I am {role}\"\n- when: \"I want {i_want}\"\n- then: \"it is done, so that {so_that}\"\n\nIts tests check that at least one story text comes back and that it carries the request's words.\n\nThe only finding along the way was one TB085: a local variable holding a `Text` was named `drafted`. I removed the variable and wrote the value inline."
  },
